	Carl J. Appellof wrote:

	>$ ucx
	>ucx> show service telnet/full
	>
	>    Will probably show you "limit: 10".
	>
	>Try
	>
	>ucx> set service telnet/limit=64


Another thing to check:

	$ UCX
	UCX> show comm

	Communication Parameters

	Local host:      axuw11                 Domain:   cern.ch

	Cluster timer:             5
	                                 Maximum     Current        Peak
	Interfaces                            10           2           2
	Device_sockets                        60           5           9
	Routes                             65535           4           4
	Services                              60           0           1
	Proxies                               20

	[Other comm. parameters left out]

Check the "Device_sockets" maximum.  On some machines the default (60
above) can be too low (this happened on our VAX 9000).  You can
increase/decrease this parameter >DYNAMICALLY< with

	$   ucx set comm/device_sockets=120

We put this in our SYSTARTUP.COM to avoid this problem in the future.

[Note that I am not positive "Device_sockets" affects in-coming
connections.  I >know< it affects outgoing connections.]

