>  Is it possible to use a VR299 monitor on a svga board? I though
>I remembered a post like this a couple of weeks ago but its off my server's
>available messages. I also check the faq's at gatekeeper.dec.com with no luck.

	This question comes up a lot and the answer is no.  The VR299 (and
others used with GPX class systems like the DS3100) is a 60Hz fixed frequency
monitor.  I know of no PC type video adapter that handles it.  The sync
signal is also not where PCs stick it (on green I think.)

>
>  Also, can a Toshiba 3401B cd-rom be used as a boot device (CD distrib) for a
>DecStation3100?

	Either the RRD43 or RRD44 is a 3401 with special firmware.  Check
the SPD for 4.4 to see if either of these is supported for booting.  The
major problem for booting may be getting the right block size.  I don't
know whether the 3401 has a dip switch to select it.

	Sam



