In article <1994Oct26.144424.25650@imag.fr>,

>I'd like to know of the interoperabilty or vendor problems, as well as the
>other possible solutions. 

  I hit one problem that p***es me off: I have a SunOS Yellow Pages
server and I configured an OSF machine to be a replica server.
Works, at least sort of. The SunOS clients are out of luck, since due
to a brilliant idea by somebody, SunOS does not use DNS if yp is running.
It wants to get BIND through YP. Obviously the OSF replica has no
clue what the SunOS client wants. Yes, I know. I can hack the libraries
on SunOS, or I can play the ypset game on the SunOS machines. Something
I did not want to do right before phasing out SunOS (question of months).
You can argue, who is to blame, but the fact is a fact: you will
encounter problems if you want to run a replica (or may be master)
YP server under OSF with SunOS clients.
  On the other hand we are much more happy with AXP than SUN (better
performance, better hardware (reliability), only one patch so far, etc.
But this only OUR enviroment and OUR usage profile.

