Should be easy.  Just plug the VT220 into the printer port of the 3100 with
the dec offset RJ45 cable for "null modem".  When the system powers up,
the firmware looks to see if there is a video terminal on the printer port.
If so, it becomes the console.  If you are trying to turn a VS3100 into
a MicroVAX 3100 to get more user licenses, however, it may not work.  The
later models had a different CPU ID for the VAXStation, and the license
Management Facility won't let you license the unit as a MicroVAX.
