In article <1994Oct20.143252.20478@gdstech.grumman.com>,
Jon Kreisler <jon@gdstech.grumman.com> wrote:
>I am about to take the plunge, converting from VAX C v3.2 to DEC C v4.0 on a 
>VAX OpenVMS v5.5-2 system.  I am aware of the problem of being unable to take
>an image created by DEC C and running it on a system only running the older
>libraries.

Not only will images not transfer, 'main()' modules compiled by DEC C 4.0
will not link on systems without the new libraries. Several people
in this group suggested work arounds for this (thanks!), but all
of them involve hacking the code in non-standard ways, or adding
assembler, or both.

What this means is you can't easily get around the problem of not
being able to distribute images to older systems by distributing
object and linking on the destination machine.

