Thomas Leitner (tom@finwds01.tu-graz.ac.at) wrote:
: I'm in the process of getting an old VAXStation 3600 which comes with:

:     - 16MB RAM
:     - monochrome monitor
:     - RA70 Disk (ca. 550.000 blocks)
:     - VMS 5.3
:     - VWS
:     - DecNet
:     
16 MB is definitely enough memory for a single user computer.  The
disk space is limited, but you can probably live with it.  If the
graphics controller is either a VCB01 or (most likely) VCB02, then
it will definitely work with either VWS or Motif.  You will note,
however, that the ~3 MIP processor (KA650-AA) is really slow with
Motif.  I have tried Motif with a MicroVAX II processor, and it
takes 12 minutes to log in and get a terminal window.  This same
operation takes ~10-15 Sec with VWS!  Your times would be 3 x faster,
or 4 minutes to log in.  This may be acceptable - you'll have to
judge.  I am staying with VWS for the present.


