Remove the disk pack using the plexiglass cover and snap the
bottom cover on.

With the top cover open, look to the rear where the heads are.  There is
a knurled knob connected to a long screw on one side or the other
(I can't remember which and there's too much stuff on top of our drives
to look right now).  Unscrew the screw and move it to the other position
(to the left or right).  I think the word "LOCK" is inscribed on the
metal head carrier.

Please, please make sure you do this.  We have had many head crashes
in the old days due to people moving these drives without locking the
heads.  Also make sure you screw down the four feet on the bottom of
the cabinet when it gets to its new location.

If my instructions don't make sense or you still have problems, let
me know and I can probably dig up an RA60 manual which lists all of
these goodies.

