To read your answerback, use the following command file
(this example actually sets your process name to a shortened version  of your
  answerback - but can be modified for your own needs)

$ans[0,8]=5
$set terminal/noecho
$read sys$command answerback /prompt="''ans'" /timeout=2/error=noanswerback
$count=0
$on error then goto plus
$plus:
$count=count+1
$pnam="''count' ''answerback'"
$pnam=f$extract(0,15,pnam)
$set mess/notext/nofac/noident/nosev
$set process/name="''pnam'"
$noanswerback:
$set mess/text/fac/ident/sev
$set terminal/echo

'ope this 'elps lad!

Mark

