In article <ORLTBL3Q@math.fu-berlin.de>, EREYES@ccr.dsi.uanl.mx (Ernesto Reyes Dorado) writes:
|>We have 3 Sable's (Alpha AXP 2100 A500MP). Each system
|>has an HSD05 Storage Works array with four RZ28's RAID 5
|>configured.

As the HSD05 itself has no RAID-5 capabilities internally, it's likely you also
have an SWXCR (RAID Array 210) RAID disk controller, if you have a RAID-5 array
configured at present...

|>We want to configure the three systems as a six  DSSI 
|>VMSCluster node (3 AXP systems and 3 HSD05).

This is fully supported, and is referred to as a tri-host DSSI configuration.
Digital supports up to 4 host CPU nodes on a DSSI bus, with a few exceptions
(see the VMScluster Software SPD, 42.18.02, for details).

|>I can connect HSD05 as DSSI nodes and all the RZ28 disks
|>are cluster wide accesible when RAID is not used.
|>
|>Is posible to connect HSD05 as DSSI nodes and configure
|>the disks as RAID level 5? Are the RAID 5 group of
|>disks cluster wide accesible or they remain as local
|>disks?

If you want multi-host access and failover of your RAID-5 array members, then
instead of using the SWXCR controller, you'll need to use the host-based
StorageWorks RAID Software for OpenVMS to form RAID-5 arrays of the disks
connected to the HSD05 controllers.  (The UPI is 2YF for per-CPU licenses or
0MG for per-disk licenses.)  By running this software on each of your 2100
systems, you will have cluster-wide access to the RAID-5 arrays, which will
continue despite the loss of any CPU node or any 1 disk out of each RAID-5
array.

For highest availability, consider putting at most 1 member of each RAID-5
array on each HSD05; that way, you can also survive a failure of any HSD05 and
continue operating.  But with only 3 HSD05s, this does limit you to 3-member
RAID-5 arrays, whose storage efficiency is only 66% (but still better than
volume shadowing (RAID-1) at 50%).
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 Keith B. Parris, StorageWorks Host-Based Software Team, Digital Equip. Corp.



