In article <38461r$3do@asbe05.phx1.aro.allied.com>, pjt@asbt14.phx1.aro.allied.com (Philip J. Tait) writes:
> We want to move a TU80 from a PDP11/44 to an SMS LSI-11/73 Q bus system.  We
> have an M7196 module (described as a TSV05 interface).  Is this the right
> board for the job?  If so, does anyone have information on the two banks
> of 10 DIP switches on the M7196?

  It might work, it might not. Both the M7454 (Unibus TU80 controller) and
the TSV05 controller speak "Pertec Formatted", but the TSV05 knows some things
about the TS05 drive (such as the speed select bit) that don't apply to the
TU80. You could try it and see.

  Probably the "best" way to do this is with a Dilog DQ132 controller. The
DU132 is the same hardware as the M7454, but with "generic" firmware. The
DQ132 is the Q-bus version of that card. It's long obsolete (the newer cards
have big buffers and speak MU rather than MS), so you should be able to get
one pretty cheaply if the TSV05 controller doesn't work.

