: upgrades. The problem is this. He has lost his license key paperwork on
: both products. They are version 5.3-1 I think of the O.S. 

: Is there a way around it? is the license management facility overridable.

Ummmm....  Uh, I probably shouldn't post this, but uh,
just put the following in the *.com files that are triggered by 
systartup_v5.com :
$ assign/table=lmf$license_table -
".............  < this is 80 .'s in a row, count them>......." -
LMF$DEC_VAX-VMS
and repeat for each licensed product.
there should be exactly 80 periods in a row between the " " s
This is DEC's own back door - don't ask me why!  Don't ask me how long
it will work (up to what version, that is).
But it works now.

And, yes, DEC should be able to replace the license PAK's, but they won't
make it easy for you.  They are usually blue pieces of paper in a crinkled
blue folder.  They look like stock certificates, with lots of engraved
curliques preprinted on the paper.  They have some individual printing
in black laser printer ink, with the words DIGITAL PAK at the top in
large letters, and a 16 character code at the bottom.

The ethernet problem could be a hardware problem, or it could be the selector
switch that sets the unit for AUI or BNC ethernet connection.

				Jon



