Hey, now THERE's an idea.....

by the way, not *ALL* dec terminals do control chcracters in the answerback,
most notable, the VXT2000 series.   The problem with windows-based
terminals is, when setting up options (like answerback), <CR> is tied
to the "[OK]" part of the window options, and NOT the text being 
answered.

After bitching about this nonstop, DEC finally came up with
a solution, involving "#" and digits.  Enter "#" and a hex code
to generate things like <CR>, <LF>, etc.

(MANY vendors assume the answerback from the terminal ends in CR!)

