David Bell (dcb@tauon.ph.unimelb.edu.au) wrote:
: On a 874-E power controller that ususally controlls RA81 drives
: and the like several of the outputs are switchable.
: This is controled by a three pin plug that goes in the J9 J10 J11 J12
: sockets from other parts of the CPU .
: Question which pins do I need to short in order to switch on the 
: switchable outputs? ( I don't have a manual)

Yes, you guessed right. You short pins 1 and 2 if I remember right.
The power control supplies the power.  I think if you short 2 to 3 it
is emergency power off.

: And What is the difference between the three switch settings
: On , Local on, Remote on. I think I know but I thought I'd better 

Local on means all power is on as long as the plug is plugged in.
Off (the center postition) means the power is off, period.
Remote On means the 3 contact power control plug controls the switched
outlets.



