SCP,70MGR-CP0204:; ucx sho export

File System                             Host name

/vmsfiles/nfs                           *
/workdisk/build/scp_7-0_base/work       MICROJET

-------------------------------------
SCP,70MGR-CP0204:; ucx sho serv mount
-------------------------------------

Service             Port  Proto    Process          Address            State

MOUNT                 10  UDP      UCX$NFS          0.0.0.0            Enabled

==============================================================================

        On the SUN, a mount was done from the root login (using a shell):

==============================================================================
VMS_C4=/home/cp0204
VMS_C4_BASE_WORK=/workdisk/build/scp_7-0_base/work

umount -v ${VMS_C4}
mount -tv nfs cp0204:${VMS_C4_BASE_WORK} ${VMS_C4}

mount -p
..
cp0204:/workdisk/build/scp_7-0_base/work /home/cp0204    nfs rw           0 0
==============================================================================


        A UNIX "ls" in "/home/cp0204" shows the VMS "SCP_WORK" directories.
A directory called "WWS_SUN.DIR;1" was created on VMS (had to use "70MGR"
because of permissions).  Then from the SUN, I could "cd wws_sun" and use
vi to create a file (I called it "i_hope_this_works.c").
From VMS, I could "TYPE I_HOPE_THIS_WORKS.C" and read the contents just fine.

Then I added some code:


====================================================================
/*
