:         1 DZQ11 4 Line ASYNC Mux card           (M3106)
:         1 TK50 Tape controller and drive
:         1 RQDX# SCSI Disc controller (no drive) (M7555)

Another has already answered the location of the cards adequately, but
you should know that the RQDX(3?) disk controller is an MFM disk controller
which will take MFM drives ONLY.  No SCSI in there.  The TK50 uses a
SCSI-like interface, but it is not SCSI protocal compatible.  The RQDX2
controller takes RD51 and RD52 disk drives (30 and 40 MB if my memory
serves me). The RQDX3 controller takes RD51 through RD53 drives - up to
80 MB.  You may have trouble using this system with modern versions
of software, they're too big to fit on those small disks.
I have a MV-II, but I have upgraded the disks 3 times.  If you have
any problems with it, let me know, I have complete manuals for it.
The console port on the CPU card is connected to a little square plate
with two rotary switches, a toggle switch a single LED digit, and a
25 pin RS232 plug.  This is a CK630-AA (Cabinet Kit).  This is where you
plug in the system console, to run diagnostics and boot the system.

				Jon



