We have an AXP 2100 A500MP, with one processor in it. It's running
VMS 6.1 ( the factory installed version )

I recently added the single port SCSI controller to this system (the
DEC-branded ADAPTEC 1742A). It shows as PKB0 on the system and has one
device on it, an external HP DAT drive (MKB500). I installed the board and
ran ECU, I didn't change any settings from the default. I disabled the
floppy controller on the board. I also removed the on-board SCSI
terminators and attached the board to the second SCSI bus on the 
in-cabinet disk shelf (using the Digital supplied cable). There are
currently no drives in any of the internal drive slots on this bus. 

Since doing this I get errors logged from the disks on the original
SCSI controller ( the one on the multi function card that comes with
the system ). These only seem to occur during the boot process, I
haven't seen any during normal operation. Typically the error
manifests as a "Device is in Mount verification" error, followed in
a second or two by a "Mount verification has completed" message. I've
attached a typical error log entry associated with this. This controller
has 3 devices on it, an RZ28, an RZ28B and an RRD43. I see errors on
both the RZ28 and the RZ28B.

As this started when the new board was installed I suspect either a
problem with the new board, or a configuration problem of some kind
(or possibly a bug in the way the system handles multiple SCSI controllers)

Has anyone else seen this, and have you figured out what causes it? The
system is under warranty so I can call Field Service in if necessary, but
since it so far seems to be a transient problem during booting it hasn't
seemed to be worth the trouble.

Thanks in advance.


