Timothy D. Shoppa x4256 (shoppa@almach.caltech.edu) wrote:
: Does anyone know exactly which DIP switch or jumper to set to change
: the unit number for the TU80 (CDC Keystone)?  Also, are there any jumpers
: to set a "timeout" for the blower?  One of my TU80's seems to turn
: off the blower after about 30 seconds of inactivity, while on the other
: one the blower runs constantly while a tape is loaded.

The air compressor power down is enabled in the following fasion:
Tape must be unloaded.
Jumper W1 on backup memory (on servo control PCB) must be in 1-2 position
to enable changing memory.  The servo control board is accessed this way:
With power ON, access rear of drive.  There are two sets of boards,
three big ones to the left (as seen from the rear) and three small ones
to the right.  There are two white knobs at the top and bottom of the card
cage between the sets of cards.  rotate the knobs up, so that they unscrew
from the right (smaller) cards.  This will allow you to swing the outer edge
of these cards to the right.  This exposes the servo control card.  Near the
bottom middle, about two inches above the card edge connector in the bottom
middle of the card is the backup memory jumper. Toward the front of the drive
is the normal (no write) position.  Move the jumper to the rear pair of pins.

Now, press test. press step until display reads 48. press execute.
This enables the compresser timeout.  (to disable, step to test 37 and 
execute).  You should get a 00 in the display. 73 or 74 indicates the
memory write is not enabled.  75 or 76 indicates some other problem with
the memory.

Now, put the jumper back, and close the card cage.

Assuming you have the stadard Pertec interface, your drive is a 92185-01,
and the interface board (the one with the cables to the controller) is a
77023050 (etched in copper, upper front edge, left side of board)
or 77020320 (same location, I guess).
In either case, the address is set with a 4 pos dip switch in the upper
center of the board.  Sw 1 selects formatter number 0 or 1.  Off is
formatter 0.  Switches 2 and 3 select drive number 0..3
sw 2   3	drive #
  off  off	0
  off  on	1
  on   off	2
  on   on	3

Switch 4 is not used.

Other option jumpers are labeled on the cupper etch.  You may need a 
magnifier to see it.

for 77020320 board
W1	1-2	Parity disabled		2-3 Parity enabled
W2	not used
W3	in  Remote density select	out local density select
W5	in  Adaptive velocity ctrl	out CPU selects 25/75 IPS

for 77023050 board
W1	1-2 Parity not sent with data	2-3 Parity sent with data
W3	1-2 Remote Density Select	2-3 Local Density Select
W5	1-2 Adaptive Velocity Sel	2-3 CPU selects 25/75 IPS
W6	1-2 Density Status enabled	2-3 Density status disab

Hope this info is of help.  Are you using the drive on a non-DEC
system?  like to hear about it.  I have 3 of these, 2 hooked to a
MicroVAX II with a Dilog controller.  Great, but a little noisy.

				Jon




