your favorite flavor of UNIX, and then see if you can track down a copy
of the software on media you can get loaded into your machine.  I have
a VAXStation-II at home with the VCB-02 color display.  I started out
with a serial terminal, went to the VCB-01, and recently upgraded to
the color screen.  It is a 1-MIPS machine, so is probably not worth
spending a lot of money on, but it is a nice system.  It runs a lot of
stuff around my house.

