jon@gdstech.grumman.com (Jon Kreisler) writes:

>I am about to take the plunge, converting from VAX C v3.2 to DEC C v4.0 on a 
>VAX OpenVMS v5.5-2 system.  I am aware of the problem of being unable to take
>an image created by DEC C and running it on a system only running the older
>libraries.
>I would like to know if anyone has had unpleasant experiences doing this 
>conversion or if there are any other potential "headaches" to be wary of.

One thing that no one has mentioned that I've run into is the difference 
in the external model.  DEC C by default assumes that all external 
variables are globals VAX C assumes that they are in common blocks.  What 
happens is that any variables not in functions show up during the link 
step as undefined globals.  To fix this in individual instances use a 
#pragma compiler directive.  I'm at home so I don't have the exact syntax 
but,  I think the syntax should be:

#pragma external_model common block

variable declarations
.
.
.

#pragma external_model relaxed refdef

There may also be a switch on the compiler to do something like this as 
well but,  I don't know what it is.

