In article <1994Oct19.185046.1@slacvx.slac.stanford.edu>, I wrote:
[...]
>     If you want an _ugly_ solution, do the following:
> 
>     	ED*IT == "@dev:[dir]MY_EDIT %"
> 
>     where MY_EDIT.COM does _something_ like this:

        The command file I posted  would fail (semi-infinite looping) if
    invoked via the symbol ED*IT because it didn't "protect" itself from
    such  a symbol in trying to invoke the DCL _verb_ EDIT.  The command
    file either needs a SET SYMBOL/SCOPE=(NOLOCAL,NOGLOBAL) at  the  top
    (and  some  logic  to  restore  the symbol scope before exit), or it
    needs to locally define EDIT to the DCL verb, like so:

 -------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 $!  P1 contains "%", so ignore it.  Check P2 for an editor qualifier...
 $ 
 $ e_quals = ".A.AC.ACL.E.ED.EDT.F.FD.FDL.S.SU.SUM.TE.TEC.TECO.TP.TPU."
 $ l_quals = F$Length (e_quals)
 $ 
 $ If P2.Nes.""
 $ Then
 $     qual = "." + F$Edit (F$Element (1, "/", P2), "COLLAPSE") + "."
 $     If F$Locate (qual, e_quals) .Ge. l_quals		! Not found
 $     Then
 $	  P2 = "/EDT " + P2
 $     Endif
 $ Endif
 $ 
 $ Define/User Sys$Input Sys$Command
 $ Edit = "EDIT"				! protect against a symbol EDIT
 $ Edit 'P2' 'P3' 'P4' 'P5' 'P6' 'P7' 'P8'
 -------------------------------------------------------------------------------

	-Ken
