I'm not an expert here, but I don't think that NT can run on the model 3000
machines because of their bus and graphics architecture.  It would probably
require a lot of re-write of the code (more than say the AXP 150) in order to
reconize the system that it is running on.  The AXP 150 and the Sable 2100 (is
that the other unit they sell?) are based upon PC type of architecture, ie..
PCI bus, EISA bus, ISA bus slots, PC type graphics cards, PC type controller
cards for the HD, all of that stuff.  The other units (model 3000's) are not
built the same way.  They use a Turbo Channel bus system that is different by
far from what any PC's are using.  Much of the equipment is different indHside
the machine.

I don't think DEC has plans to try to port NT to those machines, but they may
put the 21064A chip into another model of the AXP 150.  I think that from what
I read in the trade rags that they are calling the project unit "Son Of
Mustang" and I hear that they might demo the prototype at Comdex or Decus.

Wouldn't that be something when they announce a machine that has a 300 mhz
chip that they begin to rate with BIP's into a box to run NT? (Or any
operating system for that matter).

Gary



