Jan Gerritse (gerritse@inter.NL.net) wrote:

: On a VT220 terminal, you can put an answer-back message in the set-up.
: Is there an escape sequence to read this message out ?

: I tried to find it in the manual, but without succes.

You need to send the terminal an ENQ character.

The following DCL command proc will work under VMS:

$!  DISPLAY_ANSWERBACK.COM
$!  Display the answerback code in the terminal you're using.
$!  Kent C. Brodie, Medical College of Wisconsin
$!
$ ENQ[0,8]=5                    !Symbol for an Escape
$ write sys$output ENQ
$ answerback = ""
$ read/time_out=2/prompt="(Inquiring terminal...)   " sys$command answerback
$ if answerback .eqs. ""
$ then
$   write sys$output "There does not appear to be an answerback for this"
$   write sys$output "device, OR the answerback does not end in C/R."
$ else
$   write sys$output "The answerback code is: ","""",answerback,""""
$ endif
$ exit

enjoy.  -kent

