>In article <CxKGH6.4A6@world.std.com> shannon@world.std.com (Terry C Shannon) writes:

>>In the interim, the $10K machine will run NT, the non-NT DEC 3000/300XL 
>>will remain the entry system.

>The AxP 150 is $6K or $7K, isn't it?  Why would someone pony up
>an extra $3K apparently just for PCI?

The 150 runs a rather old and crufty SCSI controller (adaptec 1742) and
video card (compaq Q-vision) on an EISA buss.  Given the well-documented
limits of EISA, and the potention of 21x64x parts, breaking the I/O buss
bottleneck is a pretty high priority.

That's not to say I think my axp150 is a poor performer; but there is more
performance to be had and PCI is clearly the direction of peripheral cards
for at least the next 3 to 5 years.

