Okay, here's an update 8-)

First of all, to dispell the above rumor: My port is 32 bits, and will
be for the forseeable future.  As I said; I need to maintain maximum
code compatibility with the current Linux code base, and since 64-bit
quantities are still available for computation, the only thing you get
by going to full 64-bits is 64-bit pointers.  I don't think we'll need
these for quite a while yet 8-)

Second: there's only a VERY slow, primitive hard-disk driver.  If someone
else out there has a REAL hard-disk driver, I'd like to hear about it!
Otherwise, it's essentially running off the RAMdisk right now.  I hope
to get it running off the hard disk (with the current, creaky, slow
driver) within the next few days.

Finally, the update: As of last Thursday, Linux/AXP has gotten to a shell
prompt!  I haven't ported any other utilities yet, so I can't yet *do*
much, but it's coming...

Right now I'm trying to iron out a firmware-compatibility problem that
makes this thing fail on Jensen.  After that, I'll package up a
developer's kit and make it available.

