>

  This is a desktop PDP-11 that was developed about the same time as
  the IBM PC.  It ran a modified version of RSX11M+ called POS
  (Professional Operating System).  I believe there was also a
  version of Venix (or some Unix variety) for it.  The IEEE bus
  was, and still is useful for controllling a number of lab
  instruments.

  The system isn't particularly fast.  But with POS and the DCL
  toolkit installed, you can pretty much run any old PDP11 RSX
  software.  I myself haven't used one in 5-6 years at least, and
  only know one person still running one (he's a little stubborn
  I guess, in fact he runs the first pre-release of V1.0 that was
  still vanilla RSX11M+).

  (and before you ask, I have no idea where to find a copy of POS)

