>Don't think me ignorant, but what is Open VMS and VMS?

OpenVMS is VMS with the word open in front of it.  I think this
particular naming began when versions of VMS started to include
a license to use the POSIX run-time and some commands.  Once
open a time it was merely VAX/VMS with VMS meaning Virtual
Memory System and the VAX being Virtual Address eXtension.
The early VAX systems were 32 bit virtual address machines
that borrowed much from the earlier PDP11 systems.

I'm told that in its early days VMS resembled in many ways
RSX11, one of the operating systems for the PDP11 series.

At its heart VMS is your basic vendor proprietrary operating
system, with all the fanciest features.

