Denis Fortin (fortin@IRO.UMontreal.CA) wrote:
: 	Could someone indicate to me which jumper I need to set (or remove)
: on my RZ57 so that it will automatically spin up at power on instead of
: requiring an init command?  (I've recently moved an RZ57 to my PC, and
: it's a bit of a pain to have it spin up so late in the boot cycle!)

Well, here I am, following up on my own post again :-)

I have solved my problem: somebody has sent me the answer by Email, so
I'll summarize for those of you who may be encountering similar problems:
you simply have to look at the drive from the back, and underneat the
SCSI connectors, you have a few jumpers sticking our of the PCB (under
the drive; they're bent so they face to the rear, I think they're
labelled W5 or something like that).  Well, the leftmost pair of pins
(or is it rightmost, anyway, it's pretty obvious) has a jumper across
it.  Remove it and voila! instant spin-up!

Disclaimer: I did this on my RZ57 and it works like a charm. Obviously
I'm making no guarantee that this will work for you (but I don't see why
it wouldn't!?!).

Thanks to all who Emailed!

Denis Fortin, fortin@zap.qc.ca


