Chuck Mayhall (cmayhall@satland.win.net) wrote:
: I am in need of some info on a MICROVAX II. I've had it for a while and know next to 
: nothing about it. 

First of all, I assume that this is in a BA23 enclosure. The BA23 is a Tower style,
Table top, or rack mountable enclosure. The other older microVAX enclosure is the BA123
world box with wheels and sits on the floow. The BA23 has 8 Q-bus slots, the BA123 has 
12.

Second, is the memory a full or half height card. Look at the card edge and check what
boarc it is:

	M7607		1M Half height
	M7608-AA	2M Full
	M7608-BA	4M Full
	M7609		8M Full

Load the cards into the BA23 as follows:

Slot		Left Half		Right Half		

1		KA630============================================

2		MS630============================================
				
3		DZQ11================	Empty

4		TQK50================	RQDX3====================


If your memory card is the 1M half height use:

Slot		Left Half		Right Half

1		KA630============================================

2		DZQ11================	MS630====================

3		TQK50================	Empty

4		RQDX3================	Empty

If no one played with the jumpers on the cards, the system should at
lease give you the boot prompt. 

If you can cover the copy charges, I'll snail mail a copy from my 
MicroVax Systems Maintenance Guild which covers all this.

By the way, I have a personal BA23 MicroVAX with 13M RAM, full routing
DECnet, TCP/IP, an ethernet LAN to Sun Sparc workstations that serves my
consulting business very well. This is a very good system. Just a little
slow compaired to what DEC has come out with over the past few years. 


