In article <CxJvrI.7sC@inter.NL.net>,
Jan Gerritse <gerritse@inter.NL.net> wrote:
>On a VT220 terminal, you can put an answer-back message in the set-up.
>Is there an escape sequence to read this message out ?

^E (005 ASCII that is, or ENQ)

Make sure your OS doesn't turn ^Es into <circumflex> <E> on output.
On our old RSTS system we used to send CHR$(133) with VT100s to fool
the OS, that ought to work with a 220 in 7-bit mode.  Note that there's
no guarantee that the answerback is any particular length, or that
it ends in CR, or even that there is one at all, so you'll have to
set a timeout and do a delimiterless read if you want to be bulletproof.

John Wilson


