> working (granted its a slow 35meg disk...)

  Sorry to disappoint you, but a Q540 is one of the 3 devices DEC used as the
RD52, so just telling the formatter it's an RD52 should work. The other version
of the RD52 you're likely to encounter is an Atasi 3046, which is a higher-
capacity drive, but DEC ignores part of it in order to have the same capacity
as the Q540. The third drive is the Evotek ET-5540, but none of them ever went
out as RD52's - there were far too many problems with that drive. Some of the
controllers will recognize one as an RD52, though - I have an RQDX1 that does,
for example.

