In article <7OCT199415315126@almach.caltech.edu>, shoppa@almach.caltech.edu (Timothy D. Shoppa x4256) writes:
> Does anyone know exactly which DIP switch or jumper to set to change
> the unit number for the TU80 (CDC Keystone)?  Also, are there any jumpers
> to set a "timeout" for the blower?  One of my TU80's seems to turn
> off the blower after about 30 seconds of inactivity, while on the other
> one the blower runs constantly while a tape is loaded.

  For the genuine DEC TU80, they're all Unit 0. The M7454 controller doesn't
support multiple unit numbers. If you're using the Dilog version of that
board (the DU132), you can set the unit number on the drive. I'd have to look
at the service manual for details.

  Newer TU80's and all (I think) TU81's and TU81+'s shut down the reel servo
system (both reel motors and the air handler) after a certain amount of idle
time. I think this was implemented in updated microcode on the drive.

