|>so that the Alpha could write-ahead into later frames.

One way to do this is to render your animation and save it to a disk file,
perhaps using compression to keep the data rate down, then play it back 
through the video out port (NTSC or PAL, composite or S-video) of the
Sound and Motion J300 option.  This will do JPEG decompression and output
to analog video at full video frame rates, so it doesn't matter how complex
your animation is, or how long it takes to render.

There is information available on this and Digital's other multimedia products
from Digital's Web server at 

