|>  DEC told me that a DEC 3600 with J 300 board can do image 
|>  grabbing using NTSC (640 x 480) uncompressed 
|>  at full frame rate.
|>  Using PAL (768 x 576) they told me wouldn't allow that, but 
|>  with PAL you can grab one of the two half images 
|>  at full frame rate.

To clarify, the Sound & Motion J300 will capture *both* fields of
a PAL or SECAM video signal (S-video or composite) at a full 
50 field/second rate.  For NTSC, you also have the option of having
the hardware capture both fields, deinterlace them, and give you
full frames back.  This frame mode is what is not available when working
with PAL and SECAM.

