> In article <33vjg7$u3@news.bu.edu>, kearns@buphy.bu.edu (Ed Kearns)
> writes:
> 
> ELN Pascal has a [bit] type.   You can declare a packed array [x..y] of
> [bit] and then do any standard array operations on it.  I have
> successfully used this
> technique on VME bus cards that present bit masks in status registers.  It
> was more straight forward than treating them as unsigned integers.
> 
> Hope this helps,
>  Bruce
